{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Goodbye Dinner", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Happy Memories", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe past experiences in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About the Past ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use the Simple Past tense to talk about the past events.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a particular time in the past</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">arrived</span> home at six o'clock.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">continued for some time in the past</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Everybody <span class=\\\"strong\\\">worked</span> hard to complete the job.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">several times in the past </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Most weekends we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">stayed</span> at home and played video games.</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are       finished.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.   </br>   Regular verbs end in -ed or -ied.    </br></br>  Irregular verbs change in different ways.  </br>    For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary did followed by      the verb in the base form, like, \"Did you ask \u2026 ?\"  </br>    Did is the past form of to do.   ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "already", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do something before", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I already miss them and I haven't even left yet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about tourist activities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "memory", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something you remember from the past", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My friends and I have lovely memories of our childhoods.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hang out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend time together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you want to hang out later?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sad", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be upset, unhappy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally is a little sad.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "itinerary ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the details of a trip", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Last night, I printed out the full itinerary. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Don't get me wrong", "type": "name"}, {"content": "Do not misunderstand me", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't get me wrong, I love to travel.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The Simple Past talks about actions completed in the recent or distant past.  <br />The auxiliary\u00a0<span class=\"strong\">did</span>\u00a0is used when making \u00a0<span class=\"strong\">negative</span>\u00a0statements or <span class=\"strong\">questions</span> with all verbs in the past except for modal verbs and the verb 'to be' .<br />Look at the chart to review the Simple Past tense in its different forms:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Affirmative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Negative<span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Interrogative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + verb + ed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + did not  + infinitive without to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Did + subject + infinitive without to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" She <span class=\\\"strong\\\">realized</span> that I would be away from my friends.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" She <span class=\\\"strong\\\">did not realize</span> that I would be away from my friends.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Did</span> she <span class=\\\"strong\\\">realize</span> that I would be away from my friends?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, make a list of 5 things you missed the most when you traveled.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Put the